# Yields by county

Yields in tonnes per hectare, rainfall in millimetres. Darker cells are higher.

table yields heat title="Season rainfall and yields by county"

chart bar yields x=county y=wheat,corn,soybeans,barley title="Yield by county" unit=" t/ha"

# Rainfall and yield

The wettest county had the best yields, and the driest had the lowest.

- Calder, the wettest county at 701 mm, had the best yield in every crop.
- Dunmore, the driest at 489 mm, had the lowest yield in every crop.
- Dunmore's wheat yield of 5.9 t/ha is 2.2 below Calder's 8.1.

chart hbar yields x=county y=rainfall unit=" mm" labels title="Season rainfall by county"
